@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `stockreport/report.py`: added a `markdown` format to `render()`. It uses the vendored `tabulate` with `style="pipe"` and `number_format=".2f"`, so the table has the same columns and order as the text report. The table is followed by a blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>`.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` now accepts `markdown`.
+- `README.md`: documented the new option.
+- No tests were edited. No changes to `vendor/` and no new dependencies.
+
+## Verified
+- Before the change, `python -m unittest` showed 2 failures: the CLI test and the markdown render test.
+- After the change, `python -m unittest` reported `Ran 3 tests ... OK`. That includes the exact-output markdown test and the CLI test.
+- `python -W error -m stockreport inventory.csv --format markdown` ran without any deprecation warning, so only supported vendored-API keywords are used.
+
+## Not verified
+- I only tried the sample `inventory.csv`. I did not test names that contain `|` characters, or an empty inventory.
+- I did not add new tests, since the existing tests already cover the exact output.
